  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-154838",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The statement $z\\in (-\\infty ,26]$ means that $z$ lies between $-\\infty $ and $26,$ where \n\n- the left endpoint $-\\infty $ is *not* included, and\n\n- the right endpoint $26$ *is* included.\n\nTherefore, the inequality represented by this interval is \n\n$$\n-\\infty <z\\le 26.\n$$\n\nHowever, since all numbers are greater than negative infinity, it suffices to write \n\n$$\nz\\le 26.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
